{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
  "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Halkbank",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Halkbank moved to dismiss the indictment on the ground that as an instrumentality of a foreign state, Halkbank is immune from criminal prosecution under the Foreign Sovereign Immunities Act of 1976."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Halkbank",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Halkbank also warns that if the Court concludes that the FSIA does not apply in the criminal context, courts and the Executive will lack \u201ccongressional guidance\u201d as to procedure in criminal cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Halkbank",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Halkbank contends that the indictment should be dismissed because the general federal criminal jurisdiction statute, 18 U. S. C. \u00a7 3231, does not extend to prosecutions of instrumentalities of foreign states such as Halkbank."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Halkbank",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Halkbank alternatively argues that the Foreign Sovereign Immunities Act of 1976 provides instrumentalities of foreign states with absolute immunity from criminal prosecution in U. S. courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "See Black's Law Dictionary 1119 (11th ed. 2019) (defning \u201clitigant\u201d as \u201cA party to a lawsuit; the plaintiff or defendant in a court action\u201d)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is more, Congress described the FSIA as defning \u201cthe circumstances in which foreign states are immune from suit,\u201d not from criminal investigation or prosecution. 90 Stat. 2891 (emphasis added)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In stark contrast to those many provisions concerning civil actions, the FSIA is silent as to criminal matters. The Act says not a word about criminal proceedings against foreign states or their instrumentalities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Halkbank",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Halkbank contends that \u00a7 1604 renders it immune not only from civil suits but also from criminal prosecutions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0001-0006",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "With respect to the holding of the Court of Appeals that the FSIA does not provide immunity to Halkbank, we affrm on different grounds\u2014namely, that the FSIA does not apply to criminal proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1604 is as clear as a bell and we must abide by its direction that foreign sovereigns \u201cshall be immune\u201d absent some express statutory exception."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But does this mean that courts should not be involved in making immunity determinations at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1450",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "868a92d02c0b86ce69bb94dc1b957bbbf7281b33399377945519f10ad42cafda",
      "evidence_id": "ev-868a92d02c0b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would follow those straightforward directions to the same straightforward conclusion the Second Circuit reached: This case against Halkbank may proceed."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
